>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_term_ord`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_term_ord : (term * term -> order) ->
  simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sets the order guarding permutative rewrites. An unbounded rule whose sides
are equal up to variable permutation applies only when `ord (l,r)` is
`GREATER`. Use a total, AC-compatible order. Bounded rewrites (`Once`,
`Ntimes`) are not guarded. The default is `Cond_rewr.ac_term_ord`.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> fun reverse_ord p = Cond_rewr.ac_term_ord (swap p);
>> simpLib.SIMP_CONV
     (simpLib.set_term_ord reverse_ord boolSimps.bool_ss)
     [arithmeticTheory.ADD_COMM] “a + b”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.set_cond_depth`](#simpLib.set_cond_depth),
[`BoundedRewrites.Once`](#BoundedRewrites.Once).
